Hello,

I am trying to read methylation calls from sorted Bismark alignments, but I get an error.

I first use the function processBismarkAln to produce methylation call files for each sample, e.g:

sample1 = processBismarkAln(location = "sample1_pe.sorted.bam",
                              sample.id <http://sample.id> = "sample1",
                              assembly="tair9",
                              save.context= c("CpG", "CHG", "CHH"),
                              read.context = "none",
                              save.folder=getwd(),
                              mincov = 3,
                              save.db = TRUE)

And then I use the function methRead to create a methylrawList with all samples per context, e.g:
samples_CG = methRead(location = c("sample1_CpG.txt", "sample2_CpG.txt", "sample3_CpG.txt"),
                      assembly = "tair9",
                      dbtype = "tabix",
                      pipeline = "bismark",
                      context = "CpG",
                      resolution = "base",
                      dbdir = getwd(),
                      mincov = 3 )

But I get the error:

Error in (function (classes, fdef, mtable)  :

  unable to find an inherited method for function ‘methRead’ for signature ‘"character", "missing", "character"’

The head of the files looks like:

chrBase chr base strand coverage freqC freqT

Chr1.1000036 Chr1 1000036 F 7 0.00 100.00

Chr1.1000069 Chr1 1000069 F 6 0.00 100.00

Chr1.1000113 Chr1 1000113 F 5 0.00 100.00

Chr1.1000118 Chr1 1000118 F 5 0.00 100.00

Chr1.1000170 Chr1 1000170 F 11 0.00 100.00

Chr1.1000178 Chr1 1000178 F 11 0.00 100.00

What is the problem?

Thank you,

Best regards,

Núria

